# Cursor marks for clean_all_sections.cfg — positions where cursor-sensitive
# features (completion / hover) are exercised. Coordinates are 0-indexed
# (LSP Position semantics) and match the .cfg byte offsets exactly, so the
# harness feeds the feature the same position a real editor would send.
#
# Format:  <line>:<col> <feature> <optional free-form note>
#
# The three completion marks target distinct section scopes so the golden
# proves section-resolution wiring: each scope yields a different item count
# and fingerprint (config-if, config-vlan, global config).

# hover marks ------------------------------------------------------------
4:0 hover       hostname keyword -> docstring
46:0 hover      interface keyword -> docstring
13:0 hover      'router' token -> nil (exercises the no-hover path)

# completion marks -------------------------------------------------------
47:1 completion config-if scope (inside the interface body)
39:0 completion config-vlan scope
54:0 completion global config scope (top-level line)

# documentSymbol marks ---------------------------------------------------
0:0 documentSymbol  full outline across all symbol kinds (cursor is irrelevant; 0:0 is the format's placeholder)
